WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
MARTIN OMANDER: Cloud
developer communities

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.130
are groups of like-minded
cloud developers

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:08.790
who get together on a regular
basis and teach each other,

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:14.636
learn from each other on new
cloud developer technologies.

00:00:14.636 --> 00:00:17.010
AMANDA CAVALLARO: When you
attend one of the Google Cloud

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.290
community meet-ups,
you just can talk

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.780
to people about what you're
doing, your new projects,

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.760
and you also have the
chance to talk to experts

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:24.966
and learn from them.

00:00:24.966 --> 00:00:26.340
DEMI BEN-ARI: You
can also create

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.245
some kind of communication
between different Cloud GDGs

00:00:29.245 --> 00:00:30.120
all around the world.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.570
Like we're doing Tel Aviv
together with London.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.480
It's amazing the impact that
you can give to the developer

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.375
community.

00:00:37.375 --> 00:00:39.240
VIKRAM TIWARI: As the
communities evolve

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.520
and the products evolve, our
topics also evolve with time,

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.600
including more details
or more fundamentals

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.660
of as new things get launched.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:50.070
JIRAYUT NIMSAENG: We have people
from Google sharing experience

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:52.950
with [INAUDIBLE] from the GCP.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.840
ALLINE OLIVEIRA: It's
very important for me

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.020
to starting something
specific for Google Cloud

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:02.250
because it's something new in
Brazil that is very diverse.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.759
And it's going to be different.

00:01:04.759 --> 00:01:06.300
VIKRAM TIWARI: Most
of our activities

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.530
are hands-on, where
you come in, and both

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.280
of us and our assistants go
together through the code,

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.030
and we run through exercises
and get good results.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.030
ALEXIS MOUSSINE-POUCHKINE:
Google Cloud Platform

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:19.640
has been enjoying
amazing growth recently.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.910
They give us amazing feedback
on what the products really

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:25.460
should be, trying to
make sure we address

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.410
the market as best as possible.

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:30.760
[MUSIC PLAYING]

